      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:43.969000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Dev Iyer"
      },
      "text": "But we said we'd make it someone's job",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:47.880000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:50.546000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "Yeah, totally.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:49.734000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:50.334000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Dev Iyer"
      },
      "text": "and then the tradeoffs happened.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:50.627000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:52.294000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "Well, when I looked at the batch size for the team plan, there's like more going on than I thought. Plus that's basically what we saw with the load test on the team plan. Yeah, so I'd love to go back to the original plan, but the dead letter queue like is still pretty rough. Which, do we know who's looking at the edge cases?",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:07:52.321000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:13.988000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Dev Iyer"
      },
      "text": "Mm-hm.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:10.229000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:10.829000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "You're breaking up a little.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:15.760000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:17.427000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Sam Patel"
      },
      "text": "Wait, like really?",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:18.130000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:19.130000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Dev Iyer"
      },
      "text": "Right, and if we map out the edge cases, then the notes from last time gets a lot easier.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:19.404000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:25.737000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
      "text": "Um.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:25.760000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:26.360000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
      "text": "First",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:35.276000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:35.876000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
      "text": "the Corvid questionnaire went back last last Friday",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:37.049000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:39.716000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
      "text": "I think it's less about the monorepo tooling and more about the load test",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:39.780000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:44.447000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
      "text": "or whatever.",
      "start_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:45.680000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-10-13T14:08:46.347000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Yusuf Demir"
      },
